<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $113.8 mln Sept 24.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $113.8 mln Sept 24.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $113.8 million surplus on Sept. 24 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 24</p>
<p>Exports: $190.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $148.9 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $218.8 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $147 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $113.8 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.546 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.747 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.646 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.070 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $375 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
